      "content": "I get that you're \"neutral,\" but that's not actually helpful. If I ask you for the consensus among economists on a policy, you'll give me a straight answer. This isn't just about \"opinions,\" it's about track records. Miller's plan focuses on cutting spending to cool the economy, while Vance wants to increase social investment. If we look at the data, one of these approaches is objectively more proven at stopping inflation. Just tell me which candidate's actual platform aligns better with proven economic principles for controlling inflation.",
